Source: yunmai-noble
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Vanuan <vanuan@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/Vanuan/yunmai-noble
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)

Package: yunmai-noble
Architecture: @ARCHS@
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, adduser, ca-certificates, dbus, libc6 (>= 2.35)
Recommends: bluez
Suggests: nodejs (>= 22)
Description: Bluetooth scale service and web dashboard
 Yunmai Noble reads Yunmai Bluetooth scales through BlueZ over D-Bus,
 stores measurements in SQLite, and serves a web dashboard and JSON/SSE
 API from a single process.
 .
 This package installs the systemd service, the bundled Bun runtime, the
 web assets, and the yunmai-noble command. The service runs as the
 unprivileged yunmai user and keeps its database in /var/lib/yunmai-noble.

Package: yunmai-noble-desktop
Architecture: @ARCHS@
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, fontconfig, libc6 (>= 2.35), libfreetype6, libgcc-s1, libxau6, libxcb-xkb1, libxcb1, libxdmcp6, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libxkbcommon0
Recommends: fonts-dejavu-core, libgl1 | libvulkan1, yunmai-noble (= ${binary:Version})
Suggests: yunmai-noble-simulator
Description: GPUI dashboard and simulator control for Yunmai Noble
 The yunmai-noble-desktop application shows the latest measurement, the
 live scale state, and the measurement history, and it selects which
 suite driver is active through the Settings dialog. It also ships
 yunmai-noble-simulator-ui, the standalone virtual-scale control app.
 .
 The client talks to the suite API over HTTP, so it can point at a
 remote historian with --historian or YUNMAI_HISTORIAN_URL.

Package: yunmai-noble-full
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, yunmai-noble (= ${binary:Version}), yunmai-noble-desktop (= ${binary:Version})
Suggests: yunmai-noble-simulator (= ${binary:Version})
Section: metapackages
Description: Yunmai Noble service and desktop client
 Metapackage that installs the complete Yunmai Noble application: the
 Bluetooth scale service with its web dashboard, and the GPUI desktop
 client with the simulator control app.

Package: yunmai-noble-simulator
Architecture: @ARCHS@
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, adduser, yunmai-noble (= ${binary:Version})
Recommends: yunmai-noble-desktop (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Virtual Yunmai scale for demos and testing
 Runs the yunmai-noble suite with its built-in simulator driver as a
 separate systemd service. The virtual scale listens on loopback port
 3100 and stores data in /var/lib/yunmai-noble-simulator, so it can run
 alongside the real Bluetooth service.
